1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,650
If your interviewer ever asks,

2
00:00:02,670 --> 00:00:04,930
"What is your greatest weakness?"...

3
00:00:04,950 --> 00:00:06,640
do not tell the truth.

4
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:09,500
Do not shake their hand too hard.

5
00:00:09,890 --> 00:00:11,820
Do not tell them where you live.

6
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:14,520
And never say you have no questions.

7
00:00:14,970 --> 00:00:17,790
This is Protocol 404.

8
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:20,060
There are four rules.

9
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:21,770
Follow them exactly.

10
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,340
Otherwise, you will have

11
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:25,550
to activate the emergency protocol.

12
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:27,430
Rule one.

13
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,700
Do not shake too hard.

14
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:31,730
The one on the left stands

15
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:33,800
up and holds out his hand.

16
00:00:33,910 --> 00:00:35,330
His fingers are longer

17
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:36,390
than they should be.

18
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:39,140
Everyone told you the same thing.

19
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:40,610
A firm handshake.

20
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:42,520
Show them you are strong.

21
00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:43,670
Do not.

22
00:00:43,690 --> 00:00:47,300
In that room, a firm grip is a challenge.

23
00:00:47,530 --> 00:00:49,900
And they always answer a challenge.

24
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:53,440
Squeeze, and he squeezes back.

25
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:54,880
A little harder.

26
00:00:54,910 --> 00:00:56,320
Then harder.

27
00:00:56,350 --> 00:00:58,450
He does not stop when you stop.

28
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:00,960
A candidate once gave him

29
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:03,470
the firmest handshake of his life.

30
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,120
They heard it from the waiting room.

31
00:01:06,070 --> 00:01:07,490
He signs everything with

32
00:01:07,510 --> 00:01:08,860
his left hand now.

33
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:11,160
So keep your hand soft.

34
00:01:11,470 --> 00:01:12,920
Let him hold it.

35
00:01:12,990 --> 00:01:13,950
Count to three.

36
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:16,730
He loses interest, and lets go.

37
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:18,650
He writes something down.

38
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:20,250
"Not a threat."

39
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:22,210
That is a good sign.

40
00:01:22,660 --> 00:01:23,790
Rule two.

41
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:25,920
Do not tell the truth.

42
00:01:26,370 --> 00:01:27,630
Everything you say in that

43
00:01:27,650 --> 00:01:29,500
room goes into a file.

44
00:01:29,730 --> 00:01:31,580
And the file is a map.

45
00:01:31,890 --> 00:01:33,300
A map to you.

46
00:01:33,750 --> 00:01:35,200
"Tell me about yourself."

47
00:01:35,590 --> 00:01:36,880
Say your name.

48
00:01:36,950 --> 00:01:39,680
Say one sentence about your last job.

49
00:01:39,750 --> 00:01:40,570
Then stop.

50
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:43,230
Never say you live alone.

51
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:44,990
A candidate once did.

52
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:46,870
The one in the middle wrote it down.

53
00:01:47,180 --> 00:01:48,920
Then he underlined it.

54
00:01:48,940 --> 00:01:49,760
Twice.

55
00:01:50,810 --> 00:01:52,790
Living alone means no one will

56
00:01:52,810 --> 00:01:54,790
notice when you stop coming home.

57
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:57,750
Then he leans forward.

58
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:00,500
"What is your greatest weakness?"

59
00:02:00,950 --> 00:02:03,040
Do not tell the truth.

60
00:02:03,110 --> 00:02:04,810
Your real weakness is how

61
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:06,060
they will come for you.

62
00:02:06,510 --> 00:02:07,880
One candidate said,

63
00:02:08,110 --> 00:02:09,800
"I'm afraid of the dark."

64
00:02:10,190 --> 00:02:11,610
That night, the power

65
00:02:11,630 --> 00:02:13,080
went out in his building.

66
00:02:13,470 --> 00:02:14,920
Only his building.

67
00:02:16,270 --> 00:02:18,720
Give them the answer everyone gives.

68
00:02:18,750 --> 00:02:20,320
"I work too hard."

69
00:02:20,350 --> 00:02:21,810
"I'm a perfectionist."

70
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:25,280
It is already in every file they have.

71
00:02:25,300 --> 00:02:26,830
They learn nothing new.

72
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:28,690
Rule three.

73
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:31,100
Never say you have no questions.

74
00:02:31,550 --> 00:02:33,960
At the end, they put their pens down.

75
00:02:34,430 --> 00:02:36,250
"Do you have any questions for us?"

76
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:37,800
In this room,

77
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:40,930
the interview only ends when you ask something.

78
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:43,520
Say, "No, I think you covered

79
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:45,710
everything," and look at the clock.

80
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:47,500
It goes back to nine.

81
00:02:48,350 --> 00:02:49,930
The one on the left stands

82
00:02:49,950 --> 00:02:51,880
up and holds out his hand again.

83
00:02:52,270 --> 00:02:53,480
"Thanks for coming in."

84
00:02:53,790 --> 00:02:54,980
It starts over.

85
00:02:55,430 --> 00:02:57,360
It will keep starting over.

86
00:02:57,670 --> 00:02:59,090
Every handshake.

87
00:02:59,110 --> 00:03:00,600
Every question.

88
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:02,070
Until you ask one.

89
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:05,850
One candidate said no forty times.

90
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:08,900
For him, it is still Monday, nine A.M.

91
00:03:09,950 --> 00:03:12,200
Do not ask about the salary.

92
00:03:12,510 --> 00:03:14,010
Do not ask what happened to

93
00:03:14,030 --> 00:03:15,910
the last person in this job.

94
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:18,130
Ask only this.

95
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,610
"When will I hear back?"

96
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:21,730
They stand up.

97
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:22,960
"We'll be in touch."

98
00:03:23,710 --> 00:03:25,120
Rule four.

99
00:03:25,150 --> 00:03:26,760
Emergency protocol.

100
00:03:26,990 --> 00:03:28,300
How to fight back.

101
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:31,130
If you broke even one rule,

102
00:03:31,150 --> 00:03:32,570
they will be in touch.

103
00:03:32,590 --> 00:03:34,270
Exactly as promised.

104
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:35,850
Three A.M.

105
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,210
You wake up.

106
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:40,860
Three interviewers are standing at the foot of your bed,

107
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:41,920
holding your file.

108
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:44,790
"We have a few more questions."

109
00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:47,870
Here is what does not work.

110
00:03:48,320 --> 00:03:50,170
Pretending to be asleep.

111
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:53,620
They write down, "Lacks enthusiasm."

112
00:03:54,070 --> 00:03:55,280
Screaming.

113
00:03:55,670 --> 00:03:56,720
They write down,

114
00:03:56,870 --> 00:03:58,930
"Strong communication skills."

115
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:01,990
Saying you already took another job.

116
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:04,190
They ask for the company's name.

117
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:06,630
Then they visit that company too.

118
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:10,410
There is only one thing that works.

119
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:12,970
Remember what they really are.

120
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:14,850
They are not monsters.

121
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:16,200
They are employees.

122
00:04:16,650 --> 00:04:18,230
And every employee is

123
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:20,130
afraid of the same thing.

124
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:21,600
Sit up.

125
00:04:21,620 --> 00:04:23,110
Fold your hands.

126
00:04:23,140 --> 00:04:25,150
Look straight at the middle one.

127
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,560
"Congratulations.

128
00:04:26,580 --> 00:04:27,430
You're hired."

129
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:29,330
They freeze.

130
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:30,540
In that room,

131
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:32,930
whoever makes the offer is the boss.

132
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:34,700
You just made the offer.

133
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:36,810
Their folders drop.

134
00:04:36,830 --> 00:04:38,440
They stand up straight.

135
00:04:38,510 --> 00:04:40,710
They are your employees now.

136
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:44,210
Then say the words every employee fears.

137
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:46,220
"Unfortunately...

138
00:04:46,240 --> 00:04:47,410
we're letting you go.

139
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:49,500
Effective immediately."

140
00:04:50,350 --> 00:04:52,410
Three small cardboard boxes

141
00:04:52,430 --> 00:04:53,960
appear in their hands.

142
00:04:54,030 --> 00:04:55,450
Inside each one,

143
00:04:55,470 --> 00:04:58,130
a stapler and a sad little plant.

144
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:02,100
They walk out of your bedroom one by one,

145
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:04,190
and you never give them a reference.

146
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:08,210
The next morning, one new email.

147
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:10,220
"We are sorry to hear about

148
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:12,260
the recent changes in our team."

149
00:05:12,710 --> 00:05:15,530
"We have restructured our hiring process."

150
00:05:15,980 --> 00:05:17,990
Then the doorbell rings.

151
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:19,320
Through the peephole,

152
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:21,110
three new interviewers.

153
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:22,120
One of them is

154
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:23,790
already holding out his hand.

155
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:27,000
"Welcome to the second round."

156
00:05:28,050 --> 00:05:30,970
And that was Protocol 404.

157
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:33,960
If this ever happens to you...

158
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:35,320
you know the protocol.
